# CLAUDE.md

Guidance for Claude Code (and other AI agents) working in this repository.

This project was generated from the [Meower](https://github.com/AlyxPink/meower)
template. It's a starting point, not a framework — you're meant to drift from it
freely as the project grows. Update this file as the architecture diverges.

## How to read these rules

- 🔴 **Invariant** — follow without exception. Security, data integrity, cross-layer contracts.
- 🟡 **Default** — follow unless the current task has a specific reason not to. State the reason briefly if you deviate.
- 🟢 **Preference** — apply when it serves the task. Judgment call.

Words like "always", "never", "must" inside a 🟡 or 🟢 rule describe the
*default*, not an absolute. If uncertain, ask.

## Stack & Structure

| Layer | Tech |
|-------|------|
| Web | Fiber + Templ + HTMX + TailwindCSS |
| API | Go + gRPC + PostgreSQL (SQLC) |
| Observability | OpenTelemetry + Prometheus + structured logs (charmbracelet/log) |
| Dev | Docker Compose + `wgo` (hot reload) |

**Flow**: Browser → Web (Fiber) → gRPC → API → PostgreSQL

This is a multi-module Go workspace (a root `go.work` ties the modules
together):

```
TEMPLATE_PROJECT_NAME/
├── api/                 # gRPC API server
│   ├── proto/           #   Protocol Buffer definitions (.proto)
│   ├── db/              #   SQL schema + queries → SQLC-generated Go
│   ├── observability/   #   metrics server, traced DB pool, telemetry init
│   └── server/          #   gRPC services, middleware, config, workers
├── web/                 # Fiber web server
│   ├── handlers/        #   request handlers
│   ├── views/           #   Templ templates (.templ)
│   ├── routing/         #   route registration
│   ├── router/          #   the urls-kit → Fiber registry
│   ├── sse/             #   server-sent-events hub
│   └── observability/   #   web tracing init
├── pkg/
│   ├── urls/            #   type-safe URL builder (shared by web + api)
│   └── observability/   #   shared logging + trace helpers
├── scripts/
└── go.work
```

## Quick Start

```bash
docker compose up
```

| Service | URL |
|---------|-----|
| Web | http://localhost:3000 |
| gRPC API | localhost:50051 |
| gRPC UI | http://localhost:50050 |
| pgweb (DB UI) | http://localhost:5430 |
| Mailpit | http://localhost:8025 |

`wgo` regenerates `.go`, `.templ`, `.proto`, `.sql`, and CSS/JS automatically on
change. The metrics endpoint is on `:9091/metrics`.

🟢 Prefer `go vet ./...` over `go build` during dev — faster, no stray binaries.

## Code Standards

🔴 `.go` and `.templ` files use **tabs** (enforced by `gofmt` / `templ fmt`).

🔴 **No raw SQL in Go application code** — use SQLC. Write queries in
`api/db/*.sql`, run `sqlc generate`, call the generated methods. Raw SQL is fine
in migrations, one-off scripts, and test fixtures.

🟡 Regenerate code after changing its source: `.proto` → `buf`/protoc (or
`./scripts/generate_protobuf.sh`), `.sql` → `sqlc generate`, `.templ` →
`templ generate`. Under `docker compose up`, `wgo` does this for you.

🟢 Tests use stdlib `testing` — this base avoids a testify dependency. Match that
unless you have reason to add one.

## Routing — the urls kit

🟡 Routes are defined as typed structs in `pkg/urls`, which is the single source
of truth for both URLs and Fiber patterns. Define a route once; build its URL
with `urls.X{...}.URL()` and register it with `router.Register(...)`. Rename a
route and the build breaks instead of silently 404ing.

```go
// pkg/urls — define once
type Meow struct{ ID string `param:"id"` }   // URL()="/meows/abc", Pattern()="/meows/:id"

// routing.go — register
router.Register(web, fiber.MethodGet, urls.Meow{}, handler)

// anywhere — build a link
urls.Meow{ID: id}.URL()
```

🟢 To normalize parameter values in URLs (e.g. dashless UUIDs), set
`urls.ParamTransform` once at startup. It's nil (verbatim) by default.

## Real-time — the SSE hub

🟡 `web/sse` is an in-process hub: handlers publish events to a named channel
with `app.Hub.Broadcast(channel, sse.SSEEvent{...})`, and browsers subscribe at
`/events/stream?channels=...` via the HTMX SSE extension. See the meows list +
`handlers.Meower.Create` for a worked example. The hub fans out within one web
instance; put Redis pub/sub in front of `Broadcast` for multi-instance fan-out.

## Observability

🟡 The api emits OTLP traces (gRPC, `:4317`), the web emits OTLP traces (HTTP,
`:4318`), both configure structured logging (JSON in production for Loki), and
the api serves Prometheus metrics on `:9091`. Endpoints default to localhost and
read from `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT`. Use `observability.LogWithTrace(ctx)`
to get a logger with trace/span IDs attached.

## Middleware

🟢 gRPC interceptors live in `api/server/middleware` (recovery, trace
enrichment, a Redis rate limiter). Web middleware lives in `web/middleware`
(trace enrichment, trace-ID response header). Recovery runs first in the chain.

