## Authentication

🟡 Session-based auth (login/signup/logout) lives in `web/handlers/auth.go` and
`web/handlers/middleware.go` (`AuthMiddleware`, `GuestMiddleware`,
`OptionalAuthMiddleware`), backed by the Redis session store. This is a minimal
starting point — extend it (password reset, email verification, OAuth) as
needed. *(Omitted when generated with `--no-auth`.)*
<!-- /AUTH-SECTION -->

<!-- WORKERS-SECTION -->
## Background workers

🟡 `api/server/workers` is a periodic-worker harness: implement the `Worker`
interface (`Name`/`Interval`/`Run`), register it in
`api/server/workers_wiring.go`, and the `Manager` runs it on its interval with
panic recovery. See `HeartbeatWorker` for the pattern. *(Omitted when generated
with `--no-workers`.)*
<!-- /WORKERS-SECTION -->

